{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLJkwYyGGyKMGcUE7Qgj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the one inconsistency I could reproduce. The two examples in the issue already printed the same as `pprint` on this checkout, before I changed anything.\n\nThe one I did find was `exp` with a constant negative exponent. The LaTeX printer moved it into a denominator, while `pprint` keeps it as a power. For example, `latex(exp(-2)*log(y))` gave `\\frac{1}{e^{2}} \\log{\\left (y \\right )}`, and `pprint` shows `ℯ⁻²⋅log(y)`.\n\nThe change is one line in `sympy/simplify/radsimp.py` (line 961). In `fraction(..., exact=True)`, a negative-exponent `exp` term now stays in the numerator. After the change, `latex(exp(-2)*log(y))` should print `e^{-2} \\log{\\left (y \\right )}`, but I didn't re-run that case. I only confirmed that the `x**-2.5` and `x**(3/2)` cases are unchanged.\n\nI ran `test_latex.py`, `test_simplify.py` and `test_radsimp.py` with and without the change. The same 7 tests fail both ways: 3 in `test_latex.py`, plus failures in `test_simplify.py` and `test_radsimp.py`. I didn't run the rest of `sympy/printing` or `sympy/simplify`, because that run timed out.\n\nOther negative powers still print as fractions (`x**-2.5` as `\\frac{y}{x^{2.5}}`, `pi**-2` as `\\frac{y}{\\pi^{2}}`). I left that alone because it looks like intended LaTeX behaviour, and the issue allows better output where LaTeX can do it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":33616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"output_tokens":562,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16ff7346-3c03-4343-be1c-492529a96dc7","uuid